cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or baseline evaluation suite in research, benchmarks, or technical reports, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "Open Image Enhancement, Deblurring & Pixel-Art Scaling Baseline Dataset (v1.0.0)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
# Archival DOIs (Zenodo & Harvard Dataverse) will be populated upon public release.
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
url: "https://enhancephoto.org/pixel-art-upscaler"
authors:
  - name: "Open IQA Baseline Benchmark Project"
    website: "https://enhancephoto.org"
keywords:
  - "image quality assessment"
  - "super-resolution"
  - "image restoration"
  - "deblurring"
  - "pixel art scaling"
  - "open baseline"
  - "public domain"
  - "cc0"
  - "cc-by-4.0"
abstract: "A reproducible CC BY 4.0 benchmark of 40 verified CC0 and Public Domain source images across 6 restoration and scaling tasks (archival denoising, 2x/4x upscaling, Gaussian deblurring, JPEG Q30 deblocking, historical print clarity, and 4x RGBA pixel-art scaling), paired with deterministic local open-source baseline outputs and full-reference/no-reference objective IQA metrics."
